---
import { getCollection } from 'astro:content';
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { network, forms, routes, founding, slotLine } from '../lib/network';
import { url } from '../lib/url';
import { publishedLabs, institutionsOf } from '../lib/labs';

const labs = await publishedLabs();
const institutions = institutionsOf(labs.filter((l) => l.data.tier === 'member'));
const docs = (await getCollection('docs', (d) => !d.data.draft && d.data.audience === 'public')).sort(
  (a, b) => a.data.order - b.data.order || a.data.title.localeCompare(b.data.title, 'en'),
);
---

<Base title="About" description={network.mission}>
  <h1>About</h1>
  {network.name_native && <p class="muted" lang="zh" style="margin-top:-0.3rem">{network.name_native}</p>}
  <div class="prose">
    <p class="lead">{network.mission}</p>
    <p>
      A network, not a society: no legal entity, no fees, no president. What exists is an agreement among labs to
      host seminars together, keep a public roster, share teaching material, and let any member invite a speaker on
      behalf of all. Should a legal form ever be needed, the decision will be taken openly and recorded in the charter.
    </p>

    <h2>Why</h2>
    <p>
      The field in the Greater Bay Area is spread across many campuses, a few labs each. No single department has
      the audience to justify inviting the speakers its members want to hear, and no existing society spans the
      border between Hong Kong, Macau and Guangdong. Pooling audiences and invitations solves both at once.
    </p>

    <h2>Language</h2>
    <p>
      English is the default working language, so that researchers across institutions can take part in the same
      events. Names may appear in Chinese and English, and training material may be contributed in either language
      when clearly labelled.
    </p>

    <h2>How it runs</h2>
    {founding && (
      <p class="small muted">
        Proposed arrangements, subject to confirmation by the founding labs. The{' '}
        <a href={url('docs/charter/')}>charter</a> is a draft for their ratification.
      </p>
    )}
    <dl class="facts">
      <dt>Seminars</dt>
      <dd>{slotLine}. Online on {network.seminar.platform}{network.seminar.fallback_platform ? `, ${network.seminar.fallback_platform} as fallback` : ''}.</dd>
      <dt>Hosts</dt>
      <dd>Each seminar is hosted by one member lab in turn: it invites, chairs and circulates the link.</dd>
      <dt>Coordinators</dt>
      <dd>A small group, one per institution where possible, on rotating terms. They keep the calendar, review submissions and hold the repository.</dd>
      <dt>Tiers</dt>
      <dd>Member labs are in the region; affiliates take part from elsewhere. Both reviewed before listing.</dd>
      <dt>Delisting</dt>
      <dd>On request, or when a PI leaves the region. The roster is refreshed annually.</dd>
      <dt>In the open</dt>
      <dd>Roster, calendar, charter and this site are files in a public repository. Changes are pull requests.</dd>
    </dl>
  </div>

  <h2>{founding ? 'Conveners' : 'Coordinators'}</h2>
  {network.coordinators.length === 0 ? (
    <p class="muted">To be announced.</p>
  ) : (
    <dl class="facts">
      {network.coordinators.map((c) => (
        <>
          <dt>
            {c.url ? <a href={c.url}>{c.name}</a> : c.name}
            {c.name_native && <span class="muted"> {c.name_native}</span>}
          </dt>
          <dd>{c.institution} · {c.role}</dd>
        </>
      ))}
    </dl>
  )}
  {founding && (
    <p class="small muted">Founding conveners from several institutions and cities are named here as they confirm.</p>
  )}

  {institutions.length > 0 && (
    <>
      <h2>Institutions</h2>
      <ul class="inline-list">
        {institutions.map((i) => <li title={i.city}>{i.name}</li>)}
      </ul>
      {network.host_institutions.length > 0 && (
        <p class="small muted" style="margin-top:0.75rem">Seminar series co-hosted by {network.host_institutions.join(', ')}.</p>
      )}
    </>
  )}

  <h2>Documents</h2>
  {docs.length === 0 ? (
    <p class="muted">Being drafted.</p>
  ) : (
    <dl class="facts">
      {docs.map((d) => (
        <>
          <dt><a href={url(`docs/${d.id}/`)}>{d.data.title}</a></dt>
          <dd>{d.data.summary ?? ''}</dd>
        </>
      ))}
    </dl>
  )}
  <p class="small"><a href={url('docs/')}>All documents, including coordinator handbooks</a></p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    {network.contact_email ? (
      <>
        <a href={`mailto:${network.contact_email}`}>{network.contact_email}</a>. To join the announcement list, which
        carries the meeting links, <a href={routes.followEmail}>send a short email</a>.
      </>
    ) : (
      <>
        A role address is being set up. Meanwhile, <a href={forms.issues}>open an issue</a> or ask any member PI.
        The announcement list, which carries the meeting links, is passed on the same way.
      </>
    )}
  </p>
</Base>
